1. Purpose
This template allows each jurisdiction to implement MWPTS Core without importing another country’s labour law or administrative structure. Each country profile defines local wage rules, deduction categories, support contacts, languages, and implementation notes.
2. Required profile fields
Field	Type	Required	Instruction
jurisdiction_code	enum	yes	JP, KR, TW, SG, VN or another jurisdiction code.
currency_code	enum	yes	Currency used in payslip amounts.
minimum_wage_rule_enabled	YES/NO	yes	NO when the jurisdiction has no general statutory minimum wage rule suitable for Core screening.
minimum_wage_table	array/object	conditional	Regional, sectoral, or national wage values maintained by local experts.
excluded_allowance_rules	array	recommended	Allowances excluded from minimum wage test.
premium_pay_rules	object	recommended	Overtime, night, and holiday premium pay rules where applicable.
deduction_review_threshold	decimal	recommended	Review threshold such as 0.30. This is not a legal limit unless the profile states so.
tolerance_amount	decimal	recommended	Amount used to avoid false positives from rounding.
support_contacts	array	recommended	Worker-facing consultation channels.
language_pack_codes	array	recommended	Languages used for worker-facing explanations.
profile_maintainer	string	yes	Organization or experts maintaining the profile.
profile_status	enum	yes	template, draft, pilot, validated, deprecated.

3. Five-country starting matrix
Profile	Primary role	Implementation note
JP	Domestic pilot and reference implementation	LINE, Excel MVP, support agencies, labour professionals.
KR	Korea EPS-compatible local profile	KakaoTalk bot or NGO/administrative support tools can implement local profile.
TW	Traditional Chinese and migrant-worker profile	Web application and labour bureau/broker-facing transparency tools.
SG	Itemised payslip and deduction transparency profile	Focus on payslip itemisation and worker explanation rather than general minimum wage screening.
VN	Language pack and future domestic profile	Vietnamese language pack for destination countries; domestic profile can be added by local experts.

4. Governance
Country profiles should be maintained by local experts. MWPTS Core should not present sample profile data as official legal data. Public releases must label each profile as template, draft, pilot, or validated.
